diff --git a/external/more_fonts/README-beebeeb.md b/external/more_fonts/README-beebeeb.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..37e33668d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/external/more_fonts/README-beebeeb.md
@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+# Beebeeb font bundle (task 1567, item 4)
+
+Six files, packaged the same way as `font_liberation`/`font_carlito` right next to
+this file (`UnpackedTarball_beebeeb.mk` + `ExternalPackage_beebeeb.mk`), plus an
+explicit entry in `static/CustomTarget_emscripten_fs_image.mk`'s file list (the
+`gb_emscripten_fs_image_autoinstall`/`ooo_fonts` auto-aggregation mechanism the
+*other* fonts in this directory rely on is wired through scp2's installer module
+list, which this fork's minimized WASM distro config does not build — found by
+running the build and observing `soffice.data`'s byte size not changing after
+the ExternalPackage step succeeded; fixed by listing the 6 files directly,
+matching how `fc_local.conf` and `opens___.ttf` are already listed there).
+
+Purpose: task 1567 fix-pass item 4 — non-Latin fallback (the fixture's own
+"日本語" rendered as tofu boxes) + a bundled UI font (Inter) + general symbol/
+emoji fallback, all with zero network font loading, ever.
+
+| File | Upstream | Version/commit | License |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `Inter-Regular.ttf`, `Inter-Bold.ttf` | github.com/rsms/inter, release v4.1 (`Inter-4.1.zip`) | `InterVariable.ttf`, instanced to static wght=400/700 (opsz=14) via `fonttools varLib.instancer --update-name-table`, then renamed to plain "Inter"/"Regular"/"Bold" (the release ships only a variable font + WOFF2, no static TTF) | OFL-1.1 |
+| `NotoSansJP-Regular.ttf` | github.com/googlefonts/noto-cjk, `Sans/SubsetOTF/JP/NotoSansJP-Regular.otf` (main branch) | Adobe's own "SubsetOTF" common-use Japanese subset (hiragana/katakana/Joyo-and-common kanji + Latin), NOT the full 65k-glyph unified CJK font | OFL-1.1 |
+| `NotoSansSymbols-Regular.ttf` | github.com/google/fonts, `ofl/notosansymbols/NotoSansSymbols[wght].ttf` | instanced to static wght=400 via `fonttools varLib.instancer --update-name-table` | OFL-1.1 |
+| `NotoSansSymbols2-Regular.ttf` | github.com/google/fonts, `ofl/notosansymbols2/NotoSansSymbols2-Regular.ttf` | already static | OFL-1.1 |
+| `NotoEmoji-Regular.ttf` | github.com/google/fonts, `ofl/notoemoji/NotoEmoji[wght].ttf` | instanced to static wght=400 via `fonttools varLib.instancer --update-name-table`; monochrome (no color glyph tables), per this task's own "Noto Color Emoji or a monochrome emoji font" choice — Color Emoji is tens of MB and would have blown the size budget alone | OFL-1.1 |
+
+All six: SIL Open Font License 1.1 — same license family as the Liberation/
+Carlito/other Noto fonts already bundled in this directory; no new license
+obligation for this fork (OFL text for each is in the respective upstream
+repo/release; not re-vendored here to avoid duplicate/stale copies — this
+table is the attribution record).
+
+## Why these, not the others
+
+- **Chosen: Japanese only, not the full Noto Sans CJK / SC / KR set.** The
+  reported bug (task 1567 fix-pass item 4, and the visible tofu in
+  `e2e/fixtures/office/sample.pptx`'s own "日本語" text) is specifically
+  Japanese. Simplified Chinese and Korean subsets from the same noto-cjk
+  release were measured (SC: 6.0 MB brotli, KR: 3.18 MB brotli) and would fit
+  the 15 MB ceiling combined with everything else, but leave almost no
+  margin. Deferred as a follow-up, not silently dropped — see the task file's
+  dated note for the exact numbers this decision was made against.
+- **Chosen: Adobe's "SubsetOTF" Japanese font (4.5 MB raw), not the full
+  per-language Noto Sans JP OTF (16+ MB raw).** SubsetOTF already restricts to
+  commonly-used characters (confirmed to cover the fixture's own "日本語" and
+  general contemporary Japanese text) — a hand-built custom subset via
+  `pyftsubset` was considered and not needed once this pre-subsetted upstream
+  option was found to already fit comfortably.
+- **Chosen: Noto Emoji (monochrome), not Noto Color Emoji.** Noto Color Emoji
+  embeds bitmap/COLR+CPAL color glyph data and is tens of MB even subsetted —
+  incompatible with the 15 MB ceiling for the WHOLE font set. Monochrome
+  emoji still resolves emoji codepoints to a real glyph instead of tofu,
+  which is the actual requirement (a monochrome glyph, not full-color
+  rendering, matches this task's own "Noto Color Emoji OR a monochrome emoji
+  font" either/or framing).
+- **Inter, both weights, static (not the variable font).** LO's WASM
+  FreeType/HarfBuzz build was not verified to select a specific `wght` axis
+  instance at render time (no test performed either way — this is a real
+  unknown, not a confirmed limitation); shipping fixed Regular/Bold instances
+  sidesteps that unknown entirely and is a well-understood, always-correct
+  choice for two named weights.
+
+## Size (measured, `brotli -q 11`, task 1567 fix-pass, 2026-09-27)
+
+| File | Raw | Brotli |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| NotoSansJP-Regular.ttf | 4,533,028 | 3,352,941 |
+| Inter-Regular.ttf | 342,068 | 127,425 |
+| Inter-Bold.ttf | 343,736 | 131,289 |
+| NotoSansSymbols-Regular.ttf | 185,364 | 78,976 |
+| NotoSansSymbols2-Regular.ttf | 1,233,128 | 435,925 |
+| NotoEmoji-Regular.ttf | 886,696 | 523,861 |
+| **Total** | **7,524,020 (7.18 MiB)** | **4,650,417 (4.43 MiB)** |
+
+Well under the task's 15 MB brotli ceiling (uses ~30% of the budget), with
+~10.5 MB of margin — most plausibly spent on Simplified Chinese and/or
+Korean coverage as a follow-up (see above).
